# Accessibility Testing

Apply when editing accessibility specs, axe integration, or keyboard/structure checks.

## Scope

This is **automated accessibility testing** — `@axe-core/playwright` plus keyboard navigation and structural checks.

It is **not** a complete manual WCAG audit. Never claim full WCAG conformance from a passing run.

## What to test

- Run axe rules on key pages from discovery inventory or `qa.config.json` targets.
- Keyboard focus order and visible focus indicators on interactive elements.
- Landmarks, headings hierarchy, form labels, and image alt text where detectable automatically.
- Keyboard interaction, 200% Chromium CSS zoom, and 24×24 CSS-pixel touch targets where measurable.
- Undiscovered chrome (nav, tables, images) is **NOT_APPLICABLE** with a reason — do not invent it.
- Document violations with rule ID, impact, element, and page URL in reports.

## Execution

```bash
npm run test:accessibility
```

Config: `playwright.accessibility.config.ts`  
Reports: `reports/accessibility/findings.json`, `reports/accessibility/findings.md`

## Scenario mix

| Type | Examples |
| --- | --- |
| **Positive** | Page loads with no critical axe violations |
| **Negative** | Known fixture pages with deliberate a11y defects must FAIL |
| **Boundary** | Empty states, modals, dynamic content after interaction (non-destructive) |

## Integrity

- Report real axe violations — do not suppress rules to achieve PASS.
- Distinguish **application defects** (missing labels, contrast) from **automation defects** (wrong page, timeout).
- Include accessibility findings in final report severity (see `reporting.mdc`).
- Retest after fixes with `npm run retest --source accessibility` when applicable.
